  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Validating the production and market of Planq Furniture in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombia has a strong textile producing industry, in particular in Medellin and Pereira where large international fashion brands source their products. This production leads to millions of items of textile waste per year as it often is cheaper to over-produce clothing than to limit production to avoid waste. To date there is no sustainable waste processing solution in the textile industry causing it to often end up burned, buried or on the black market. Creating awareness in the entire chain about the value and need for sustainable textile waste processing is needed to reduce its negative impact on the environment.  Dutch design studio Planq works in collaboration with Dise&#xf1;o de Holanda and Nvest to expand their business activities of furniture design and production based on their in-house developed material &#x2018;Planq Textile&#x2019; to Colombia. Planq Textile is derived from waste textile such as production waste or old uniforms. Together with Nvest and Dise&#xf1;o de Holanda, Planq is sharing Dutch innovation and knowledge to provide economic growth, local employment and environmental impact in Colombia.In order to prepare for future investments, the opening of a local production facility of Planq products in Colombia, Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) provides support to validate the Colombian market and to test the feasibility of producing locally with recycled textiles.</narrative>
  </description>
